# 13. Initialize the Master Node

Run this command only on the Master / Control Plane:

```bash
sudo kubeadm init --pod-network-cidr=10.244.0.0/16
```

The command initializes:

```text
Kubernetes API Server
Controller Manager
Scheduler
etcd
Control Plane
```

At the end, kubeadm provides a worker-node join command similar to:

```bash
sudo kubeadm join <MASTER-IP>:6443 \
--token <TOKEN> \
--discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:<HASH>
```

Save this command.

It will be required on both worker nodes.

---

# 14. Configure kubectl on Master

After `kubeadm init`, configure kubectl:

```bash
mkdir -p $HOME/.kube
sudo cp -i /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf $HOME/.kube/config
sudo chown $(id -u):$(id -g) $HOME/.kube/config
```

Test:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

Initially the worker nodes will not appear because they have not joined yet.

---

# 15. Install Calico CNI

Kubernetes requires a pod network.

Install Calico:

```bash
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/projectcalico/calico/v3.26.4/manifests/calico.yaml
```

Check:

```bash
kubectl get pods -n kube-system
```

Wait until the Calico components become healthy.

---

# 16. Join Worker Nodes

Run the `kubeadm join` command generated during `kubeadm init`.

Run it on:

```text
Worker Node 1
Worker Node 2
```

Example:

```bash
sudo kubeadm join <MASTER-IP>:6443 \
--token <TOKEN> \
--discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:<HASH>
```

Do NOT run `kubeadm join` on the master.

