# 20. Clean Kubernetes Cluster Reset

If the cluster becomes corrupted and needs to be recreated:

Run on worker nodes:

```bash
sudo kubeadm reset -f
```

Run on master:

```bash
sudo kubeadm reset -f
```

Clean CNI configuration:

```bash
sudo rm -rf /etc/cni/net.d
```

Clean Kubernetes configuration:

```bash
rm -rf $HOME/.kube
```

Restart containerd:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart containerd
```

If IPVS was used:

```bash
sudo ipvsadm --clear
```

Then recreate the cluster from the initialization stage.

> Important: `kubeadm reset` does not remove `$HOME/.kube/config`, so that file may need to be removed manually when rebuilding the cluster.

