# 39. Jenkins Docker Permission Error

Initially Jenkins produced:

```text
permission denied while trying to connect to the Docker daemon socket
```

Cause:

The Jenkins user did not have permission to access:

```text
/var/run/docker.sock
```

Resolution:

The Jenkins user was given access to Docker and verified using:

```bash
sudo -u jenkins docker info
```

Successful result:

```text
JENKINS CAN ACCESS DOCKER
```

---

# 40. Docker Client Version Error

Another error occurred:

```text
client version 1.29 is too old.
Minimum supported API version is 1.40
```

Cause:

Jenkins was using an older Docker CLI configured through the Jenkins Docker Tool installation instead of the system Docker CLI.

Resolution:

The Jenkins Docker configuration was corrected so Jenkins used the current Docker installation.

Verification:

```bash
docker --version
sudo -u jenkins docker --version
sudo -u jenkins which docker
```

Expected:

```text
/usr/bin/docker
```

---

# 41. Docker Hub Authentication

Docker Hub authentication initially failed.

The Jenkins credential was corrected to use:

```text
Docker Hub username
+
Docker Hub Personal Access Token
```

instead of relying on the Docker Hub account password.

The pipeline was then able to successfully push the image.

---

# 42. Jenkins to Kubernetes Connection Timeout

The deployment stage initially failed with:

```text
failed to download openapi

dial tcp <MASTER-IP>:6443:
i/o timeout
```

Cause:

Jenkins could not reach the Kubernetes API server on:

```text
6443
```

The issue was related to network/security-group connectivity between the Jenkins EC2 instance and Kubernetes control-plane EC2 instance.

Resolution:

Verified:

```text
Kubernetes API server
Security Group
Port 6443
Private IP connectivity
Jenkins host connectivity
```

After correcting connectivity, Jenkins successfully executed:

```bash
kubectl apply -f deployment-service.yaml
```

---

# 43. Important Lesson From Troubleshooting

For a Jenkins → Kubernetes deployment, there are three separate things that must work:

```text
1. Jenkins credentials
        |
        v
2. Jenkins network connectivity
        |
        v
3. Kubernetes RBAC permissions
```

Having correct Kubernetes credentials alone is not enough.

Jenkins must also be able to reach:

```text
MASTER_PRIVATE_IP:6443
```

